                    {
                        "sense_id": "3870ba74-c9ca-3f3a-a7ee-1e8edc7e74af",
                        "entry_id": "bf041d7f-c311-3d67-9429-cd78a71e0a72",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A small Greek restaurant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "08a2cfa6-6e7a-4ef0-878f-2fa1f0a052be",
                                "sense_id": "3870ba74-c9ca-3f3a-a7ee-1e8edc7e74af",
                                "text": "The streets of Palizzi, through which no Englishman perhaps had as yet descended, were swarming with perfectly naked, berry-brown children, and before I reached the taverna I could hardly make my way through the gathering crowd of astonished mahogany Cupids. The taverna was but a single dark room, […]; still it was a better resting-place than the hut at Condufóri, inasmuch as it was free from many intruders."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "59ed6658-02c5-443c-9e88-418ce8bc00e8",
                                "sense_id": "3870ba74-c9ca-3f3a-a7ee-1e8edc7e74af",
                                "text": "In the tavernas of Loutro I had the best octopus I’ve ever eaten, grilled simply with garlic, olive oil and sage over a charcoal fire."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
